Option 1 — Plug in a USB microphone (easiest)

Any USB mic or USB headset will show up immediately as a new card:
arecord -l    # will show card 2: USB Audio [...]

Then set in docker-compose.yml:
environment:
  - CARA_MIC=plughw:2,0
  - CARA_SPEAKER=plughw:2,0   # if it's a headset with speaker too

Option 2 — Configure ALSA UCM for the 3.5mm jack

This is the proper fix if you want to use the built-in analog jack. Run on the Jetson host (not in the container):
# Check if UCM is already present
ls /usr/share/alsa/ucm2/

# Try enabling the headset path
amixer -c 1 sset 'Headphone' unmute
amixer -c 1 sset 'Capture' unmute cap
amixer -c 1 sset 'Capture' 80%

Then retry arecord -D plughw:1,0 ... — if it produces a file larger than 44 bytes, the routing is live.

The segfault is solved either way — arecord opens cleanly, there's just nothing to record yet. Once you have a working audio source, Cara will pick it up immediately through the CARA_MIC env var.


